From 70d605f0d2fcf67b8724ddce8ddde1df1048a768 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: H-river <hujiamomomo@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 00:45:04 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] Fix curriculum not reaching the command sampler;
 tensorboard by default; pin BAM

- microduck_velocity_env_cfg.py: the twist command was built with
  `command.build = lambda env, _cmd=command: ...`, which binds the cfg object
  registered with the task. mjlab builds the env from a deep copy of it
  (load_env_cfg / tyro), and the staged curriculum edits that copy through
  command_manager.get_term_cfg("twist"), so the widened ranges at iteration
  3000 never reached the sampler. Use UniformVelocityCommandWithRotationCfg,
  whose build() uses self. Checked with rl_train/tests/check_curriculum.py:
  after the stage the sampled rotation |wz| goes 0.75 -> 1.50 (old lambda:
  stays 0.75).
- MicroduckVelocityRlCfg: logger tensorboard (wandb stalls without
  WANDB_API_KEY); pass --agent.logger wandb to opt in.
- pyproject.toml: pin better-actuator-models to rev 0007411 (the doc-branch tip
  already in uv.lock) so a re-lock cannot drift; uv.lock re-generated, no
  version changes.
- .python-version: 3.13 (the version every policy here was trained with).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
